ACFMorningMeeting - Oil relief- President Trump said on Sunday that further US attacks on Iran were highly unlikely while talks progressed. Brent eased, reducing one source of inflation pressure before the European open. Friday’s strong US jobs report however is evidence that supports a Fed rate rise.

Opens - FTSE 100 futures were 10,691.3 (+0.23%) and DAX futures 25,863.0 (-0.05%); EURO STOXX 50 futures at -0.2%. US S&P 500 futures were +0.6% in a later Asian-market report; Japan’s Nikkei and Taiwan’s cash markets rebounded strongly. $STOXX $FTSE $FTMC $DAX $CAC $DJI $GSPC $IXIC

Stock Watch - Nvidia $NVDA: The board said Sunday that it is investigating reports CEO Jensen Huang was targeted by a foreign intelligence officer via a honey trap. Out-of-hours shares and near $180.30 early Monday, about -3.4% against Friday’s $186.64 Nasdaq close. The investigation adds leadership uncertainty ahead of the US open; the board says it has no reason to believe company secrets were compromised. Irish Residential Properties REIT $IRES.IR faces a 17:00 GMT deadline today for Barings to announce a firm bid or walk away. The board said it would be minded to recommend a firm offer at €1.386 a share, subject to due diligence and agreed terms. This remains a possible offer, not a completed bid.

Commods - Brent $97.49/bbl in early trading and WTI $90.18/bbl  on easing Iran supply fears. Spot GOLD $4,123.46/toz at 04:28 GMT (+1.4%) as lower oil eased inflation concerns. Dec COPPER futures were $6.3378/lb (+1.24%). Latest Friday US COCOA was $5,155/MT (-0.50%). ICE raw SUGAR #11 was 18.25¢/lb (-1.67%) on Friday; ICE Arabica COFFEE was 280.15¢/lb (+1.08%) on Friday.

Data Focus - Friday’s US October payrolls rose by 165,000; markets now await Tuesday’s US consumer-price report. Today’s European calendar includes the November Sentix investor-confidence release. ACFView: cheaper oil does, over time, help re-adjust inflation expectations downwards, but a sustained European equity rebound needs rate-sensitive shares to build upward momentum in the face of stronger US employment.

